      en: "St. Paul's Church ruins in Melaka are the remains of a Portuguese chapel built in 1521. It was later expanded by the Dutch and used as a church. After the 19th century, it fell into disrepair. The ruins sit atop St. Paul's Hill, offering views of the city. The open tomb of St. Francis Xavier is a notable feature; he was briefly buried here. The site is part of the UNESCO World Heritage listing for Melaka.",
